Instance icons in icons/ are carved from the Prism Launcher binary
(prismlauncher.exe), (c) Prism Launcher contributors, licensed GPL-3.0-only.

Our workspace is already GPL-3.0-only, so the carved GPL assets stay under
the same license. The carved directory itself lives outside this repo and is
never moved; only the mapped PNGs listed below were copied here under
canonical names.

These are *instance* icons: the Minecraft-themed art a user picks per instance,
and recognises from Prism. The launcher's own chrome (rail, dialogs, inline
buttons) is not carved art at all — it is drawn as tintable vectors in
`crate::glyphs`. The toolbar PNGs that used to sit here (play, kill, minus,
check, help, about, folder, update, refresh) were removed when the chrome moved
to vectors, because a bitmap cannot take the colour of the button it sits in.

Verified visual mapping (carved filename -> meaning -> canonical name):
- 128x128_5178_169.png = chicken head -> chicken_legacy.png
- 50x50_1246_137.png = enderman head -> enderman_legacy.png
- 128x128_18345_174.png = enderpearl orb -> enderpearl_legacy.png
- 48x48_4526_119.png = grass block -> default.png and grass.png
  (byte-identical copies; Prism's default icon IS the grass block)
- 32x32_405_107.png = dirt -> dirt.png
- 32x32_757_103.png = steve head -> steve.png
- 32x32_1361_109.png = creeper -> creeper.png
- 32x32_228_108.png = TNT -> tnt.png
- 32x32_2270_93.png = yellow gear -> gear.png
